  "articleBody": "When your child is arrested, it's totally normal to feel overwhelmed and scared. The most important thing is to act quickly to protect their rights and future. First off, don't let them talk to anyone without a lawyer present. Kids, especially, can say things that are misunderstood or used against them without realizing the impact. You'll want to find out what exactly they're being accused of and whether they're being held or released. Having a skilled juvenile defense attorney on your side from the very beginning can make a huge difference in how the case unfolds. They can advise you on what to say and what not to say, ensuring your child's legal protections are upheld. It’s also wise to prepare for the possibility of a court appearance and discuss potential outcomes with an attorney. Remember, the goal is always to minimize the impact on your child’s life and opportunities. An attorney can help explore options like diversion programs or strategies to protect their record. Taking these steps early can really shape a more positive path forward for your family.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-26"
